{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000201",
  "title": "GPU Mandelbrot Set",
  "created_at": "2026-03-21T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-03-21T00:00:00Z",
  "shared_cargo_toml": "[dependencies]\nironpad-cell = \"0.1\"\n\n[profile.release]\nopt-level = 1\nlto = false\ncodegen-units = 16\n",
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_0",
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Introduction",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "# GPU Mandelbrot Set 🖥️\n\nThis notebook renders the Mandelbrot set using **WebGPU compute shaders**, with an automatic CPU fallback for browsers without WebGPU support.\n\nThe GPU version runs a WGSL compute shader that evaluates each pixel in parallel on the GPU, delivering massive speedups over CPU rendering.",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_1",
      "order": 1,
      "label": "GPU Mandelbrot – Full View",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use ironpad_cell::prelude::*;\n\nlet shader = r#\"\n    @group(0) @binding(0) var<storage, read> uniforms: array<f32>;\n    @group(0) @binding(1) var<storage, read_write> output: array<vec4<f32>>;\n\n    @compute @workgroup_size(16, 16)\n    fn main(@builtin(global_invocation_id) id: vec3<u32>) {\n        let width = u32(uniforms[0]);\n        let height = u32(uniforms[1]);\n        if id.x >= width || id.y >= height { return; }\n\n        let center_x = uniforms[2];\n        let center_y = uniforms[3];\n        let zoom = uniforms[4];\n        let max_iter = u32(uniforms[5]);\n\n        let aspect = f32(width) / f32(height);\n        let x0 = center_x + (f32(id.x) / f32(width) - 0.5) * zoom * 2.0 * aspect;\n        let y0 = center_y + (f32(id.y) / f32(height) - 0.5) * zoom * 2.0;\n\n        var x = 0.0;\n        var y = 0.0;\n        var iter = 0u;\n\n        loop {\n            if iter >= max_iter { break; }\n            let x2 = x * x;\n            let y2 = y * y;\n            if x2 + y2 > 4.0 { break; }\n            y = 2.0 * x * y + y0;\n            x = x2 - y2 + x0;\n            iter = iter + 1u;\n        }\n\n        let idx = id.y * width + id.x;\n\n        if iter == max_iter {\n            output[idx] = vec4<f32>(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0);\n        } else {\n            let t = f32(iter) / f32(max_iter);\n            let r = 0.5 + 0.5 * cos(6.28318 * (t + 0.0));\n            let g = 0.5 + 0.5 * cos(6.28318 * (t + 0.33));\n            let b = 0.5 + 0.5 * cos(6.28318 * (t + 0.67));\n            output[idx] = vec4<f32>(r, g, b, 1.0);\n        }\n    }\n\"#;\n\nlet center_x: f32 = -0.5;\nlet center_y: f32 = 0.0;\nlet zoom: f32 = 1.0;\nlet max_iter: f32 = 256.0;\n\nlet canvas = GpuCanvas::new(800, 600, shader, &[center_x, center_y, zoom, max_iter])\n    .with_fallback(|x, y, uniforms| {\n        let width = uniforms[0];\n        let height = uniforms[1];\n        let center_x = uniforms[2] as f64;\n        let center_y = uniforms[3] as f64;\n        let zoom = uniforms[4] as f64;\n        let max_iter = uniforms[5] as u32;\n\n        let aspect = width as f64 / height as f64;\n        let x0 = center_x + (x as f64 / width as f64 - 0.5) * zoom * 2.0 * aspect;\n        let y0 = center_y + (y as f64 / height as f64 - 0.5) * zoom * 2.0;\n\n        let mut zx = 0.0_f64;\n        let mut zy = 0.0_f64;\n        let mut iter = 0u32;\n\n        while iter < max_iter {\n            let zx2 = zx * zx;\n            let zy2 = zy * zy;\n            if zx2 + zy2 > 4.0 { break; }\n            zy = 2.0 * zx * zy + y0;\n            zx = zx2 - zy2 + x0;\n            iter += 1;\n        }\n\n        if iter == max_iter {\n            (0, 0, 0)\n        } else {\n            let t = iter as f64 / max_iter as f64;\n            let r = (0.5 + 0.5 * (6.28318 * (t + 0.0)).cos()) * 255.0;\n            let g = (0.5 + 0.5 * (6.28318 * (t + 0.33)).cos()) * 255.0;\n            let b = (0.5 + 0.5 * (6.28318 * (t + 0.67)).cos()) * 255.0;\n            (r as u8, g as u8, b as u8)\n        }\n    });\n\nCellOutput::from(canvas)\n",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_2",
      "order": 2,
      "label": "GPU Mandelbrot – Seahorse Valley Zoom",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use ironpad_cell::prelude::*;\n\nlet shader = r#\"\n    @group(0) @binding(0) var<storage, read> uniforms: array<f32>;\n    @group(0) @binding(1) var<storage, read_write> output: array<vec4<f32>>;\n\n    @compute @workgroup_size(16, 16)\n    fn main(@builtin(global_invocation_id) id: vec3<u32>) {\n        let width = u32(uniforms[0]);\n        let height = u32(uniforms[1]);\n        if id.x >= width || id.y >= height { return; }\n\n        let center_x = uniforms[2];\n        let center_y = uniforms[3];\n        let zoom = uniforms[4];\n        let max_iter = u32(uniforms[5]);\n\n        let aspect = f32(width) / f32(height);\n        let x0 = center_x + (f32(id.x) / f32(width) - 0.5) * zoom * 2.0 * aspect;\n        let y0 = center_y + (f32(id.y) / f32(height) - 0.5) * zoom * 2.0;\n\n        var x = 0.0;\n        var y = 0.0;\n        var iter = 0u;\n\n        loop {\n            if iter >= max_iter { break; }\n            let x2 = x * x;\n            let y2 = y * y;\n            if x2 + y2 > 4.0 { break; }\n            y = 2.0 * x * y + y0;\n            x = x2 - y2 + x0;\n            iter = iter + 1u;\n        }\n\n        let idx = id.y * width + id.x;\n\n        if iter == max_iter {\n            output[idx] = vec4<f32>(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0);\n        } else {\n            let t = f32(iter) / f32(max_iter);\n            let r = 0.5 + 0.5 * cos(6.28318 * (t + 0.0));\n            let g = 0.5 + 0.5 * cos(6.28318 * (t + 0.33));\n            let b = 0.5 + 0.5 * cos(6.28318 * (t + 0.67));\n            output[idx] = vec4<f32>(r, g, b, 1.0);\n        }\n    }\n\"#;\n\nlet center_x: f32 = -0.745;\nlet center_y: f32 = 0.186;\nlet zoom: f32 = 0.005;\nlet max_iter: f32 = 512.0;\n\nlet canvas = GpuCanvas::new(800, 600, shader, &[center_x, center_y, zoom, max_iter])\n    .with_fallback(|x, y, uniforms| {\n        let width = uniforms[0];\n        let height = uniforms[1];\n        let center_x = uniforms[2] as f64;\n        let center_y = uniforms[3] as f64;\n        let zoom = uniforms[4] as f64;\n        let max_iter = uniforms[5] as u32;\n\n        let aspect = width as f64 / height as f64;\n        let x0 = center_x + (x as f64 / width as f64 - 0.5) * zoom * 2.0 * aspect;\n        let y0 = center_y + (y as f64 / height as f64 - 0.5) * zoom * 2.0;\n\n        let mut zx = 0.0_f64;\n        let mut zy = 0.0_f64;\n        let mut iter = 0u32;\n\n        while iter < max_iter {\n            let zx2 = zx * zx;\n            let zy2 = zy * zy;\n            if zx2 + zy2 > 4.0 { break; }\n            zy = 2.0 * zx * zy + y0;\n            zx = zx2 - zy2 + x0;\n            iter += 1;\n        }\n\n        if iter == max_iter {\n            (0, 0, 0)\n        } else {\n            let t = iter as f64 / max_iter as f64;\n            let r = (0.5 + 0.5 * (6.28318 * (t + 0.0)).cos()) * 255.0;\n            let g = (0.5 + 0.5 * (6.28318 * (t + 0.33)).cos()) * 255.0;\n            let b = (0.5 + 0.5 * (6.28318 * (t + 0.67)).cos()) * 255.0;\n            (r as u8, g as u8, b as u8)\n        }\n    });\n\nCellOutput::from(canvas)\n",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_3",
      "order": 3,
      "label": "GPU vs CPU Comparison",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "source": "use ironpad_cell::prelude::*;\n\nlet shader = r#\"\n    @group(0) @binding(0) var<storage, read> uniforms: array<f32>;\n    @group(0) @binding(1) var<storage, read_write> output: array<vec4<f32>>;\n\n    @compute @workgroup_size(16, 16)\n    fn main(@builtin(global_invocation_id) id: vec3<u32>) {\n        let width = u32(uniforms[0]);\n        let height = u32(uniforms[1]);\n        if id.x >= width || id.y >= height { return; }\n\n        let center_x = uniforms[2];\n        let center_y = uniforms[3];\n        let zoom = uniforms[4];\n        let max_iter = u32(uniforms[5]);\n\n        let aspect = f32(width) / f32(height);\n        let x0 = center_x + (f32(id.x) / f32(width) - 0.5) * zoom * 2.0 * aspect;\n        let y0 = center_y + (f32(id.y) / f32(height) - 0.5) * zoom * 2.0;\n\n        var x = 0.0;\n        var y = 0.0;\n        var iter = 0u;\n\n        loop {\n            if iter >= max_iter { break; }\n            let x2 = x * x;\n            let y2 = y * y;\n            if x2 + y2 > 4.0 { break; }\n            y = 2.0 * x * y + y0;\n            x = x2 - y2 + x0;\n            iter = iter + 1u;\n        }\n\n        let idx = id.y * width + id.x;\n\n        if iter == max_iter {\n            output[idx] = vec4<f32>(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0);\n        } else {\n            let t = f32(iter) / f32(max_iter);\n            let r = 0.5 + 0.5 * cos(6.28318 * (t + 0.0));\n            let g = 0.5 + 0.5 * cos(6.28318 * (t + 0.33));\n            let b = 0.5 + 0.5 * cos(6.28318 * (t + 0.67));\n            output[idx] = vec4<f32>(r, g, b, 1.0);\n        }\n    }\n\"#;\n\nlet center_x: f32 = -0.5;\nlet center_y: f32 = 0.0;\nlet zoom: f32 = 1.0;\nlet max_iter: f32 = 256.0;\nlet (width, height) = (800u32, 600u32);\nlet uniforms = [center_x, center_y, zoom, max_iter];\n\nlet fallback = |x: u32, y: u32, uniforms: &[f32]| -> (u8, u8, u8) {\n    let width = uniforms[0];\n    let height = uniforms[1];\n    let center_x = uniforms[2] as f64;\n    let center_y = uniforms[3] as f64;\n    let zoom = uniforms[4] as f64;\n    let max_iter = uniforms[5] as u32;\n\n    let aspect = width as f64 / height as f64;\n    let x0 = center_x + (x as f64 / width as f64 - 0.5) * zoom * 2.0 * aspect;\n    let y0 = center_y + (y as f64 / height as f64 - 0.5) * zoom * 2.0;\n\n    let mut zx = 0.0_f64;\n    let mut zy = 0.0_f64;\n    let mut iter = 0u32;\n\n    while iter < max_iter {\n        let zx2 = zx * zx;\n        let zy2 = zy * zy;\n        if zx2 + zy2 > 4.0 { break; }\n        zy = 2.0 * zx * zy + y0;\n        zx = zx2 - zy2 + x0;\n        iter += 1;\n    }\n\n    if iter == max_iter {\n        (0, 0, 0)\n    } else {\n        let t = iter as f64 / max_iter as f64;\n        let r = (0.5 + 0.5 * (6.28318 * (t + 0.0)).cos()) * 255.0;\n        let g = (0.5 + 0.5 * (6.28318 * (t + 0.33)).cos()) * 255.0;\n        let b = (0.5 + 0.5 * (6.28318 * (t + 0.67)).cos()) * 255.0;\n        (r as u8, g as u8, b as u8)\n    }\n};\n\n// Time the GPU path.\nlet gpu_start = Stopwatch::new();\nlet gpu_canvas = GpuCanvas::new(width, height, shader, &uniforms)\n    .with_fallback(fallback);\nlet output = CellOutput::from(gpu_canvas);\nlet gpu_ms = gpu_start.elapsed_ms();\n\n// Time the CPU path for comparison.\nlet cpu_start = Stopwatch::new();\nlet full_uniforms = [width as f32, height as f32, center_x, center_y, zoom, max_iter];\nlet mut pixels = Vec::with_capacity((width * height) as usize);\nfor y in 0..height {\n    for x in 0..width {\n        pixels.push(fallback(x, y, &full_uniforms));\n    }\n}\nlet cpu_ms = cpu_start.elapsed_ms();\n\nlet speedup = if gpu_ms > 0.0 {\n    format!(\"{:.1}x\", cpu_ms / gpu_ms)\n} else {\n    \"\\u{221e} (instant)\".to_string()\n};\n\nlet report = format!(\n    \"## \\u{23f1}\\u{fe0f} Rendering Comparison (800\\u{00d7}600, 256 iterations)\\n\\n\\\n     | Path | Time |\\n\\\n     |------|------|\\n\\\n     | GPU  | {:.0} ms |\\n\\\n     | CPU  | {:.0} ms |\\n\\n\\\n     **Speedup: {}**\\n\\n\\\n     > Note: GPU time includes shader compilation on first run. \\\n     Subsequent runs are faster.\",\n    gpu_ms, cpu_ms, speedup\n);\n\noutput.with_display(report)\n",
      "cargo_toml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_4",
      "order": 4,
      "label": "Explore Further",
      "cell_type": "Markdown",
      "source": "## Explore Further\n\nTry modifying the parameters above to explore different regions of the Mandelbrot set:\n\n- **Elephant Valley**: center = (-0.1, 0.65), zoom = 0.02\n- **Spiral**: center = (-0.7463, 0.1102), zoom = 0.005\n- **Mini Mandelbrot**: center = (-1.768, 0.001), zoom = 0.0001\n\nIncrease `max_iter` for deeper zooms to see more detail.",
      "cargo_toml": null
    }
  ],
  "description": "Mandelbrot set rendered with WebGPU compute shaders, with CPU fallback.",
